  "sourceState": "Revision 8 preserves the four-operation IFormEngine and completes all 80 source cases plus all 38 migration-gap cases. Current capability/identity stays fail-closed through action-bound identifiers, fresh expiry checks after Party resolution, current-role authority, and conditional browser/job composition. The built-in single-process file adapter uses an exclusive lifetime lock, authenticated versioned frame headers, SHA-256-checksummed append-only payloads, fsync-before-index mutation, preflight identity uniqueness, and in-process delivery leases. It truncates only authenticated incomplete final frames and refuses complete-frame corruption. Abrupt separate-process tests prove durable submission/audit/outbox replay and pending-projection recovery. The authoring host boundary compiles rules and guards, validates bounded policy, and uses atomic register-and-publish before exposing a revision. The focused Forms Engine suite is 152/152. A disposable HTTP authoring host directly references only Harborline.Foundation.Forms.Engine, resolves its seven-artifact transitive closure, exercises valid/rule-rejected/policy-rejected requests, and proves zero source/project fallback or assembly ambiguity.",
